{"created": "2026-07-30T16:43:15.308171+00:00", "modified": "2026-08-10T08:54:03.147477+00:00", "id": 21706797, "conceptrecid": "21570993", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21706797", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.21570993", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21706797", "metadata": {"title": "Line-Graph Signature Beyond the 2-Core: Exact Counterexamples, Rooted Response, and Extremal Constructions at Fixed Cyclomatic Number", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21706797", "publication_date": "2026-07-30", "description": "<p>The manuscript proves an exact pendant-forest reduction, a parity property for rooted-tree responses, a singular attachment lemma in the graph-port setting, and a rank-one criterion determining when a pendant leaf increases the line-graph signature.</p>\n<p>It establishes the universal upper bound s(L(G)) &le; c(G). Together with the constructive lower bound, this gives floor((c+1)/2) &le; f(c) &le; c, so f(c) is finite and its maximum is attained for every cyclomatic number c. The sharper inequality 2s(L(G)) &le; c(G)+1 remains a conjecture.</p>\n<p>The load-bearing mathematical certificates and principal computational results were independently checked. The repaired R2 graph6 package corrects labeled graph6 serialization; the previous edge-list calculations remain valid.</p>\n<p>Andrea Paone and Marco Paone contributed equally to this work.</p>\n<p>Status: Preprint; not peer reviewed.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Paone, Andrea", "affiliation": "Independent Researcher. Project association: Aletheia Technologies, an independent research project", "orcid": "0009-0003-6194-948X"}, {"name": "Paone, Marco", "affiliation": "Independent Researcher. Project association: Aletheia Technologies, an independent research project", "orcid": "0009-0001-6792-879X"}], "keywords": ["line graph", "graph signature", "graph inertia", "spectral graph theory", "signless Laplacian", "cyclomatic number", "2-core", "rooted response", "Schur complement", "extremal graph theory", "exact computation"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.21499790", "relation": "isSupplementedBy", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.21534809", "relation": "isSupplementedBy", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.2139/ssrn.7192558", "relation": "isIdenticalTo", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}], "version": "1.3", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "communities": [{"id": "aletheia-technologies"}], "relations": {"version": [{"index": 2, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "21570993"}}]}, "notes": "<p>Version 1.3, revised on 30 July 2026. Just grammar forms</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Version 1.2, revised on 29 July 2026, preserves the first-version date of 27 July 2026. It incorporates the universal upper bound s(L(G)) &le; c(G), and hence floor((c+1)/2) &le; f(c) &le; c; updates obsolete statements about the finiteness of f(c); updates the targeted related-work discussion; and includes the repaired R2 graph6 certificates. The R2 repair corrects the labeled graph6 serialization; the previous edge-list calculations remain valid. The sharper inequality 2s(L(G)) &le; c(G)+1 remains a conjecture.</p>\n<p>Status: Preprint; not peer reviewed.</p>"}, "title": "Line-Graph Signature Beyond the 2-Core: Exact Counterexamples, Rooted Response, and Extremal Constructions at Fixed Cyclomatic Number", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21706797", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21706797", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21706797?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21706797", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21706797", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.21706797", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21706797/draft